Third-party data

The store under store/ is generated from public bibliographic sources and is
published under the same licence as the code. It contains short quoted excerpts
from the publications it documents -- at most about 300 characters each, with
the source and a link to the publication recorded alongside every one -- kept as
the evidence for why each publication is listed. Those excerpts remain the
property of their respective copyright holders and are reproduced here as
attributed quotations. Full text and abstracts are never stored in this
repository; they live only in a local download cache that is not committed.

Bibliographic metadata comes from OpenAlex (CC0), Crossref, Europe PMC, NCBI
PMC, PRIDE/ProteomeXchange and bioRxiv/medRxiv, each used through its public
API under that service's own terms.
